  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Building Bridges for Peace in Kibera (YOBBPEK)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Poverty in Kibera  is one of the  major impediments to peace building &amp; conflict transformation as more than &#xbe; of the residents live on less than $1 a day. Women , especially female headed households, unemployed youth, children mainly OVCs and  HIV infected persons  are  the  most  affected. Since the  after  math  of  2007 post election violence marred by distraction of  property and  many  forms  of  livelihoods , the youth most  of  whom are unemployed,  have  resulted to engage themselves in  violence and related ills. Women&#x2019;s role as peace keepers was also a gap identified in the fast phase. 
Youth Building Bridges for Peace in Kibera (YOBBPEK) programme is an initiative of Kenya Youth Foundation and Kibera Community Youth Programme launched in 2007 with the financial support of CAFOD.  The goal of the project was to entrench inclusive community based approach in healing, reconciliation, peace building and conflict transformation in Kibera slums using grass root strategies such as music extravaganza, participatory theatre, peace clubs, village forums for peace and conflict transformation; and action research which plays an important role in community development as it helps in identifying gaps/hindrances to meeting community needs.  CAFOD&#x2019;s  in-depth organizational review whose recommendations were to the effect that KYF internally rebuild institutional systems. This project is purely formulated as an exit strategy which will cover  Jan 2014- Dec 2014  &#xa3; 15,000.
The Project is premised on the following specific objectives:
1. Sustaining Village Peace &amp; Governance Dialogue Structures in Kibera towards enhancing &amp; amplifying the role &amp; voices of women &amp; youth in Kibera.  This will consolidate the gains made in the previous period in establishment of village structures that have been instrumental in peace building.  More groups are to be formed on voluntary basis so to take over the work of KYF at the end of the project.
2. Enhance community based innovative action research, training, documentation and dissemination of stories of change/case studies on peace building &amp; conflict transformation, governance &amp; poverty reduction in Kibera : As this an exit, KYF purpose to involve communities in research and documentation of best practices, significant positive changes and conflict dynamics that will inform subsequent engagement beyond the project period.
3. Strengthen fundraising &amp; institutional capacity of implementing organization:  The project will enhance organizational development of KYF on areas of strategic planning, development of HR and Finance manual, ICT systems and staff capacity building.
4. Strengthen and Expand Effective Networks on Peace Building, Conflict Transformation, Governance &amp; Community development. As a strategy for pooling synergies, KYF will still reach out to like-minded organizations as it has previous done.</narrative>
  </description>
